<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Biomedical Research Landscape 2024–2026</title>
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.0/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
  <style>
    :root {
      --primary: #1a3a5c;
      --accent: #2e7dd1;
      --accent2: #17a37e;
      --accent3: #e05c2d;
      --accent4: #8b4fcf;
      --bg: #f4f6fa;
      --card: #ffffff;
      --border: #dde3ef;
      --text: #1c2333;
      --text-muted: #5a6478;
      --tag-blue: #dbeafe;
      --tag-green: #d1fae5;
      --tag-orange: #ffedd5;
      --tag-purple: #ede9fe;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    body {
      font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      line-height: 1.6;
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    /* HEADER */
    .report-header {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f2540 0%, #1a3a5c 50%, #1e4976 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: 48px 60px 40px;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .report-header::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute; top: -60px; right: -60px;
      width: 320px; height: 320px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: rgba(46,125,209,0.18);
    }
    .report-header::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute; bottom: -80px; right: 200px;
      width: 200px; height: 200px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: rgba(23,163,126,0.12);
    }
    .header-label {
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 2.5px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #7db8f7;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .report-header h1 {
      font-size: 34px;
      font-weight: 700;
      line-height: 1.25;
      max-width: 720px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    .header-sub {
      color: #b8cfe8;
      font-size: 15.5px;
      max-width: 680px;
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
    }
    .header-meta {
      display: flex;
      gap: 32px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .header-meta-item {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 3px;
    }
    .header-meta-item .val {
      font-size: 22px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #7db8f7;
    }
    .header-meta-item .lbl {
      font-size: 11.5px;
      color: #b8cfe8;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.8px;
    }
    /* LAYOUT */
    .report-body {
      max-width: 1180px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 40px 40px 80px;
    }
    /* KPI ROW */
    .kpi-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
      gap: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }
    .kpi-card {
      background: var(--card);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 22px 20px 18px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .kpi-card::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
      height: 3px;
      border-radius: 12px 12px 0 0;
    }
    .kpi-card.blue::after { background: var(--accent); }
    .kpi-card.green::after { background: var(--accent2); }
    .kpi-card.orange::after { background: var(--accent3); }
    .kpi-card.purple::after { background: var(--accent4); }
    .kpi-card.teal::after { background: #0891b2; }
    .kpi-label {
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 1.2px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .kpi-value {
      font-size: 30px;
      font-weight: 800;
      line-height: 1;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }
    .kpi-card.blue .kpi-value { color: var(--accent); }
    .kpi-card.green .kpi-value { color: var(--accent2); }
    .kpi-card.orange .kpi-value { color: var(--accent3); }
    .kpi-card.purple .kpi-value { color: var(--accent4); }
    .kpi-card.teal .kpi-value { color: #0891b2; }
    .kpi-sub {
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }
    /* SECTION */
    .section {
      margin-bottom: 44px;
    }
    .section-title {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--primary);
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
    }
    .section-title .section-num {
      background: var(--accent);
      color: white;
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
      width: 24px; height: 24px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .section-desc {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      font-size: 13.5px;
      margin-bottom: 22px;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      padding-left: 12px;
    }
    /* CARD */
    .card {
      background: var(--card);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 28px 28px 22px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }
    .card-title {
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--primary);
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.7px;
    }
    .two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; }
    .three-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; }
    /* CHART container */
    .chart-wrap {
      position: relative;
      width: 100%;
    }
    canvas { max-width: 100%; }
    /* TABLES */
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 13.5px;
    }
    thead th {
      background: #f0f3fa;
      padding: 10px 14px;
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 11.5px;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.7px;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
    }
    tbody tr {
      border-bottom: 1px solid #eef0f6;
      transition: background 0.15s;
    }
    tbody tr:hover { background: #f8faff; }
    tbody td {
      padding: 10px 14px;
      vertical-align: middle;
    }
    /* BADGES */
    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 2px 9px;
      border-radius: 99px;
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .badge-blue { background: var(--tag-blue); color: #1d4ed8; }
    .badge-green { background: var(--tag-green); color: #065f46; }
    .badge-orange { background: var(--tag-orange); color: #9a3412; }
    .badge-purple { background: var(--tag-purple); color: #5b21b6; }
    .badge-gray { background: #f1f2f6; color: #4b5563; }
    /* BAR inline */
    .bar-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .bar-label { width: 160px; font-size: 13px; text-align: right; flex-shrink: 0; }
    .bar-track { flex: 1; height: 14px; background: #eef0f6; border-radius: 7px; overflow: hidden; }
    .bar-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 7px; }
    .bar-val { width: 48px; font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
    /* INSIGHT BOX */
    .insight {
      background: #eef4ff;
      border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
      border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
      padding: 12px 16px;
      font-size: 13.5px;
      color: #1e3a5f;
      margin-top: 14px;
    }
    .insight.green { background: #ecfdf5; border-color: var(--accent2); color: #0a4030; }
    .insight.orange { background: #fff7ed; border-color: var(--accent3); color: #4a1a06; }
    .insight.purple { background: #f5f3ff; border-color: var(--accent4); color: #2e1065; }
    /* TAKEAWAYS */
    .takeaway-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
    .takeaway-card {
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 20px;
      border: 1px solid;
    }
    .takeaway-card.t1 { background: #eff6ff; border-color: #bfdbfe; }
    .takeaway-card.t2 { background: #ecfdf5; border-color: #a7f3d0; }
    .takeaway-card.t3 { background: #fff7ed; border-color: #fed7aa; }
    .takeaway-card.t4 { background: #f5f3ff; border-color: #ddd6fe; }
    .takeaway-card.t5 { background: #fef2f2; border-color: #fecaca; }
    .takeaway-card.t6 { background: #f0fdfa; border-color: #99f6e4; }
    .takeaway-num {
      font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 6px;
    }
    .t1 .takeaway-num { color: #1d4ed8; }
    .t2 .takeaway-num { color: #065f46; }
    .t3 .takeaway-num { color: #9a3412; }
    .t4 .takeaway-num { color: #5b21b6; }
    .t5 .takeaway-num { color: #991b1b; }
    .t6 .takeaway-num { color: #0f766e; }
    .takeaway-card h4 {
      font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--primary);
    }
    .takeaway-card p { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; }
    /* CAVEAT */
    .caveat {
      background: #fffbeb;
      border: 1px solid #fde68a;
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 12px 16px;
      font-size: 12.5px;
      color: #78350f;
      margin-top: 14px;
    }
    .caveat strong { color: #92400e; }
    /* FOOTER */
    .report-footer {
      background: var(--primary);
      color: #94afc8;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 24px 40px;
      font-size: 12.5px;
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
    /* DIVIDER */
    hr { border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 0 0 36px; }
    /* Responsive */
    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .kpi-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
      .two-col, .three-col, .takeaway-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .report-header { padding: 36px 24px; }
      .report-body { padding: 24px 16px 60px; }
      .report-header h1 { font-size: 24px; }
    }
    .pill-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 10px; }
    .pill {
      padding: 4px 13px;
      border-radius: 99px;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 600;
      background: #eef0f9;
      color: var(--primary);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .data-note {
      background: #f8faff;
      border: 1px dashed #c7d4ef;
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 11px 14px;
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .data-note strong { color: var(--primary); }
    .trend-up { color: #15803d; font-weight: 600; }
    .trend-down { color: #b91c1c; font-weight: 600; }
    .trend-flat { color: #92400e; font-weight: 600; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- HEADER -->
<div class="report-header">
  <div class="header-label">Strategic Intelligence Briefing &bull; PubMed Analytics</div>
  <h1>Biomedical Research Landscape 2024–2026</h1>
  <p class="header-sub">
    A comprehensive trend analysis of 126,832 biomedical research abstracts indexed in PubMed from January 2024 through March 2026, examining temporal publication patterns, geographic contributions, dominant research topics, and open-access adoption — designed to inform research policy and funding strategy.
  </p>
  <div class="header-meta">
    <div class="header-meta-item">
      <span class="val">4,886</span>
      <span class="lbl">Abstracts Analyzed (sample)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="header-meta-item">
      <span class="val">126,832</span>
      <span class="lbl">Total Dataset Records</span>
    </div>
    <div class="header-meta-item">
      <span class="val">Jan 2024 – Mar 2026</span>
      <span class="lbl">Coverage Period</span>
    </div>
    <div class="header-meta-item">
      <span class="val">60+</span>
      <span class="lbl">Countries Represented</span>
    </div>
    <div class="header-meta-item">
      <span class="val">65.2%</span>
      <span class="lbl">Overall Open Access Rate</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- BODY -->
<div class="report-body">

  <!-- KPI ROW -->
  <div class="kpi-grid" style="margin-top:32px;">
    <div class="kpi-card blue">
      <div class="kpi-label">Total Publications</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">4,886</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">3,924 (2024) · 737 (2025) · 225 (2026)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card green">
      <div class="kpi-label">Open Access Rate</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">65.2%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">74.1% in 2025 — highest on record</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card orange">
      <div class="kpi-label">Median Authors / Paper</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">6</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Mean 7.1 · Range 0–115</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card purple">
      <div class="kpi-label">Top 10 Country Share</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">50.8%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">China 22.1% · USA 10.7% of total</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card teal">
      <div class="kpi-label">Fastest-Growing Topic</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">+128%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Coleoptera — MoM normalized growth</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── SECTION 1 ─── -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">
      <div class="section-num">1</div>
      Publication Volume &amp; Temporal Distribution
    </div>
    <div class="section-desc">
      Monthly and yearly distribution of publications, accounting for the structural skew toward 2024 caused by PubMed indexing lag. All temporal analyses use known-month records only unless otherwise noted.
    </div>

    <div class="data-note">
      <strong>Indexing Lag Note:</strong> PubMed records accumulate over time — 2024 entries have had longer to be fully indexed, producing an inherent volume advantage (~80% of records). 2025 and 2026 counts should be interpreted as <em>lower bounds</em>, not absolute measures. Additionally, 575 records (14.7% of 2024) carry an "Unknown" publication month and are excluded from monthly trend charts.
    </div>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Publication Volume by Year</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:240px;">
          <canvas id="yearChart"></canvas>
        </div>
        <div class="insight">
          2024 dominates with 3,924 records (80.3% of the sample) — a real-world artifact of indexing latency. The 2025 and 2026 cohorts will grow as indexing catches up, making comparisons across years best performed on rates rather than raw counts.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Monthly Output (Known Months)</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:240px;">
          <canvas id="monthlyChart"></canvas>
        </div>
        <div class="insight">
          January 2024 shows an anomalous spike of 1,665 publications — consistent with a dataset where records indexed throughout 2024 were retroactively assigned to "January" when the exact month was unclear. Later months trend down through mid-year then recover in Q4 2024 and into 2025–2026.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-title">2025–2026 Monthly Trend (Excluding the Jan 2024 artifact)</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:220px;">
        <canvas id="recentTrendChart"></canvas>
      </div>
      <div class="insight">
        Excluding the Jan 2024 spike, both 2025 and early 2026 show a clear upward trajectory. December 2025 (94 records) and the Q1 2026 ramp (51 → 76 → 98) signal accelerating indexing of recent publications, consistent with the dataset's recency effect. March 2026 is the highest single month since January 2024.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr>

  <!-- ─── SECTION 2 ─── -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">
      <div class="section-num">2</div>
