  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-title">
      <div class="section-num">6</div>
      Key Takeaways &amp; Strategic Implications
    </div>
    <div class="section-desc">
      Synthesized findings for research policy, funding prioritization, and institutional strategy. Ordered by estimated strategic impact.
    </div>

    <div class="takeaway-grid">
      <div class="takeaway-card t1">
        <div class="takeaway-num">Priority Finding 1 — Open Access</div>
        <h4>OA Adoption Has Crossed a Tipping Point</h4>
        <p>The 2025 open-access rate of <strong>74.1%</strong> — up 10 percentage points from 2024 — signals that open publishing is becoming the majority norm rather than the exception. Seven of the top 15 journals by volume are OA mega-journals or preprint servers. Policy mandates (NIH, EU Horizon) appear to be producing measurable structural shifts. Funding agencies should treat OA compliance infrastructure as table-stakes, not optional.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="takeaway-card t2">
        <div class="takeaway-num">Priority Finding 2 — Geographic Power</div>
        <h4>Asia-Pacific Bloc Controls ~35% of Global Output</h4>
        <p>China alone accounts for 22.1% of the dataset, with the Asia-Pacific region (China, Japan, India, South Korea, Australia) collectively contributing roughly 35%. India's YoY share growth from 3.3% (2024) to 8.0% (2025) is the strongest national acceleration in the dataset. Strategic funders should model engagement frameworks that assume Asia-Pacific parity, not marginal contribution.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="takeaway-card t3">
        <div class="takeaway-num">Priority Finding 3 — Topic Momentum</div>
        <h4>Post-COVID Research Decline Creates Funding Gaps</h4>
        <p>COVID-19 dropped 28% in normalized topic share from 2024 to 2025, after dominating the dataset as the single largest topic. This creates a reallocation opportunity — and risk. Research infrastructure built up during the pandemic (rapid-response platforms, surveillance networks, global consortia) may be underutilized. Funders should evaluate whether pandemic-era capacity can be redeployed toward emerging infectious disease preparedness.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="takeaway-card t4">
        <div class="takeaway-num">Priority Finding 4 — Collaboration Norms</div>
        <h4>High-Impact Research Is Multi-Author by Default</h4>
        <p>With a median of 6 authors per paper and a mean of 7.1 across nearly 5,000 records, solo authorship is the exception. Preprints — the most collaborative format at median 9 authors — also carry the highest OA rates. Grant structures designed around individual PI models may misalign with how biomedical science is actually organized. Team-science funding mechanisms deserve increased emphasis.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="takeaway-card t5">
        <div class="takeaway-num">Priority Finding 5 — Emerging Topics</div>
        <h4>MicroRNAs &amp; Lung Neoplasms Show Durable Growth</h4>
        <p>After filtering for minimum threshold (≥5 records in 2024), MicroRNAs show an 18% normalized growth rate into 2025, and Lung Neoplasms / MRI show modest but consistent gains. These signals are modest in this sample size but consistent with broader field-level trends in RNA therapeutics and precision oncology imaging. They represent credible investment targets for translational research pipelines.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="takeaway-card t6">
        <div class="takeaway-num">Priority Finding 6 — Data Quality</div>
        <h4>Indexing Lag Structurally Distorts Year-over-Year Comparisons</h4>
        <p>The 80/15/5 split across 2024/2025/2026 is a PubMed indexing artifact, not a reflection of real output. 2025 and 2026 counts are lower bounds and will grow. Any policy decision benchmarking "2025 output decline" against 2024 would be methodologically unsound. Internal datasets should be refreshed quarterly and normalized rates should be preferred over raw counts in all annual comparisons.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-top:24px;background:#f8faff;">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--primary);">Recommended Strategic Actions</div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin-top:8px;">
        <div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.7px;margin-bottom:6px;">Short-Term (0–12 months)</div>
          <ul style="list-style:none;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--text-muted);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;">
            <li>▸ Audit OA mandate compliance across funded portfolios</li>
            <li>▸ Map COVID-related infrastructure for reallocation feasibility</li>
            <li>▸ Engage India as an emerging strategic research partner</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent2);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.7px;margin-bottom:6px;">Medium-Term (1–3 years)</div>
